<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_features",
    "Some things are faster said than typed. On a phone the composer offers a Record strip: speak for up to a minute, and the recording is attached to your message like any other file."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_microphone}>{dgettext("help_features", "Recording One")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_features",
    "Press Record and allow the microphone when the browser asks. The clock beside it counts up while you speak. Attach ends the take and adds it to the message, where it waits with any other attachment until you press Send; Discard throws it away and the microphone is released either way."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_warning}>
  {dgettext("help_features", "A Minute, and Then It Stops")}
</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_features",
    "A take ends itself at sixty seconds and is attached as it stands. Past a minute it stops being something the other person can take in the middle of a conversation — which is what writing is for."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_tab_display}>{dgettext("help_features", "Where It Is Offered")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_features",
    "On a phone, and only in a browser that can record. On a desktop the file picker beside the input already attaches an audio file, so nothing is missing there."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_link}>{dgettext("help_features", "See Also")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  <.help_link topic="feature-message-attachments">
    {dgettext("help_features", "Message Attachments")}
  </.help_link>
</p>
